    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d207">

                <pb facs="0473" n="445" xml:id="pg445"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">315/3–1853: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Republic of China</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Rankin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Department
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">priority</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Taipei</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1953-03-18T18:00:00+08:00">March 18, 1953—6
                            p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>973. Re press reports Soviet would accept Madame Pandit or Benegal Rau as
                    Secretary General UNO. Foreign Minister informed me Chinese delegate Security
                    Council instructed veto proposal if made formally.</p>
                <p>Foreign Minister hopes necessity for such action will not arise and that US may
                    prevent matter from coming to vote.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rankin</hi>
                    </signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
